.TH QTPARTED 1 "October 2026" "QtParted 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qtparted \- partition editor for Qt 6 based on libparted
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qtparted
.RI [ device | image ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qtparted
is a graphical partition editor. It shows the partitions of the disks of the
system, lets the user queue changes (create partition tables, create, delete,
format, resize, move, copy and check partitions, set flags, partition names,
file system labels and UUIDs) and applies them in one
go, with a detailed log of every step.  It also opens, closes and resizes LUKS
encrypted partitions, mounts and unmounts file systems, turns swap on and off
and activates LVM Volume Groups; these actions are applied immediately.
.PP
The
.B qtparted
command is a launcher that runs the program with root privileges through
.BR pkexec (1).
.PP
Without arguments all disk devices are scanned. Devices or disk image files
given on the command line restrict the scan to them. On image files only the
partition table can be changed; attach the image with
.B losetup -P
to create file systems on it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the command line help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.zanac.qtparted.policy
polkit action used by the launcher.
.TP
.I /etc/fstab
mount points offered by the \fBMount on\fR action.
.TP
.I /usr/share/qtparted/translations/qtparted_\fIlang\fP.qm
optional translation overriding the one built into the program.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANG, LANGUAGE, LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES
language of the user interface (English, Italian, German, French, Portuguese and Brazilian Portuguese are
included).  The
launcher passes them to the program.
.SH NOTES
The user manual is built into the program: \fBHelp \(-> Contents\fR (F1).
